  "comparison": "Dependency-only, immutable workspace, and source-refreshing workspace caches on identical source commits and job commands. Existing caches start at the last recorded key-changing producer; refreshed caches start at the immediately preceding source commit. The chronological window is the last twelve commits of the previous fixed thirty-commit replay, selected before timing runs.",
  "strategy": "Three read-only PR-like replicas precede cache production at each eligible source commit. A writable producer runs for every commit, including docs-only changes skipped by the PR planner. For uv commits whose PR policy enables writes, this producer represents the first PR writer and is followed by a separate exact-hit main-like replay, since Depot shares caches across branches. Otherwise the producer represents main. All runs use workflow_dispatch on one experiment branch, isolated by experimental cache prefixes. Initial seeds are excluded from timing. Execution includes post-save steps and excludes queues.",
